    "answer": {
      "short": "Survivorship bias: only returning planes were observed; planes that failed to return are missing. Hits in sparsely marked areas, such as the engines or cockpit, may have been more likely to prevent return, so extra armour should protect those areas.",
      "worked": "The sample contains only planes that survived and returned, excluding those that failed to return. This is survivorship bias. The red marks show damage that returning planes survived. Hits in areas with few or no marks, such as the engines or cockpit, may have been more likely to prevent return. Extra armour should therefore protect those vulnerable areas.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
